# Issue 008: Add option to enforce f, g reciprocation

**Status:** Done

## Feature Overview
Our math shows that in a converged training $f$ should converge to an equal expression to $-g$, even if not explicitly instructed to.

Many runs shows this - apart from the tail (in observable space parameters terms) areas in which the dataset statistics are low, and there convergence is harder.

To show this, and to test if we get any different t_dist statistics when it's so to validate our estimation of the effective DoF, we would like to add a boolean configuration parameter "train__f_g_reciprocation", such that:
- When off (default, also for backwards compatibility) the training is done as it is now.
- When toggled on, calling the prediction of g network would just return $-f$.

## Acceptance criteria
- A new boolean configuration parameter, that defaults to false, and toggles the effect of the $g$ nn operation.
- Usage of the `DifferentiatingModel` class should remain the same, regardless of internal implementation or mode.

## Remarks and Caveats
- Current functionality should not change if none of the configuration files was changed, relative to before this implementation.

## Completion

Added the opt-in `train__f_g_reciprocation` flag, defaulting to false. When enabled, all g evaluations return negative f evaluations through the shared model-estimate path used by training and prediction. When toggled on, avoid having $g$ network calculations that would consume time and eventually not be used. That being said, minimal construction one-time code can be tolerated for the sake of simplicity of our implementation.